<title>JAPAN: Current forex rate may not cause trade woes - Toyota.</title>
<headline>Current forex rate may not cause trade woes - Toyota.</headline>
<dateline>NAGOYA, Japan 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's top carmaker Toyota Motor Corp said on Friday that current foreign exchange rates are unlikely to cause trade problems between Japan and the United States.</p>
<p>&quot;The current levels are unlikely to cause such problems,&quot; a Toyota executive told reporters in the western city of Nagoya when asked whether current forex levels will cause any trade problems between the two nations.  </p>
<p>The Toyota executive also said that a dollar/yen rate of between 110 yen and 120 yen was an appropriate level for the Japanese car industry, repeating the view offered by Toyota president Hiroshi Okuda earlier this week.</p>
<p>The dollar stood at around 113.75 yen as of 0518 GMT.</p>
</text>
